From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/26] egl: Zink on surfaceless without DRM

eglInitialize tries the hardware drivers, then Zink, then software.
On the surfaceless platform the first two probe DRM devices only, so
where there are none (iOS) Zink is never reached: the software step
without DRM would load swrast, or with LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE Zink, which
then looks for a CPU Vulkan device.

When Zink is asked for (eglInitialize's second step, or
MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE=zink) and no DRM device has a driver, run
Zink without a DRM device on the Vulkan device it finds: KosmicKrisp on
iOS. This is also the path build/mesa-host-test takes on a workstation
whose DRM devices have no driver in the build.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-11-mesa-gl-ios-build.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c
index 424d6ee..b82763e 100644
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c
@@ -519,6 +519,16 @@ dri2_initialize_surfaceless(_EGLDisplay *disp)
       _eglLog(_EGL_DEBUG, "Falling back to surfaceless swrast without DRM.");
       driver_loaded = surfaceless_probe_device_sw(disp);
    }
+   /* When no DRM device has a driver (on iOS there are no DRM devices),
+    * Zink, which eglInitialize tries when the hardware probe finds nothing,
+    * runs on whatever Vulkan device it finds (KosmicKrisp on iOS).
+    * LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE is not the way there: it would make Zink look
+    * for a CPU device.
+    */
+   if (!driver_loaded && disp->Options.Zink && !disp->Options.ForceSoftware) {
+      _eglLog(_EGL_DEBUG, "Zink on surfaceless without a DRM device.");
+      driver_loaded = surfaceless_probe_device_sw(disp);
+   }
 
    if (!driver_loaded) {
       err = "DRI2: failed to load driver";
